{"step_index":516,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T23:44:39Z","thinking":"**Reviewing the Pipeline**\n\nI've been evaluating the feedback. Drag and drop functionality seems solid, no problems there. However, a major issue is the lack of a log viewer for processes; it's clear the user needs to see the terminal output of the pipeline to improve workflow. I'm focusing on that.\n\n\n**Addressing User Feedback**\n\nI'm now prioritizing the terminal output log viewer for active processes, as the user desires. I misunderstood the placement initially; it needs to be on the active process screen, not just in Settings. The jump to results displaying zeros is another bug; it should wait for process completion. Also, I'm refactoring the UI to eliminate the vertical scrollbar, making it more flexible. Finally, I need to ensure processes are added to the history screen immediately upon starting.\n\n\n**Refining Workflow Behavior**\n\nI'm now investigating History interaction to fix state persistence issues with the \"New Process\" screen. I also need to address handling duplicate file submissions, potentially warning or redirecting. My priority also includes ensuring all terminal output is in English, as Arabic text displays poorly for the user, and adding a safety dialog on exit if background processes exist. Further, I will add an optional multi-language toggle if it is easy.\n\n\n**Implementing Progress Bars**\n\nI am now adding a staged progress bar for the pipeline, with distinct stages: \"Reading Files,\" \"Extracting PDFs,\" \"Matching,\" and \"Saving.\" I am working on the JavaScript side and ensuring the processing overlay updates accordingly. I am also planning on updating the exit confirmation as well. I'm focusing on providing more informative feedback.\n\n\n**Fixing Layout & Behavior**\n\nI'm now prioritizing the layout and behaviors. The main focus is fixing the scroll issue by setting the CSS for a full viewport height and internal scrolling. The next major task is to clear the form after submission. I'm also implementing a duplicate process check in the backend for `start_process`, verifying completed or reviewing processes with the same files. Finally, I'm refactoring the `submitProcess()` method to eliminate jumps to results.\n\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"type d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\templates\\index.html | findstr -n -A 20 \"function submitProcess\"","Cwd":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy","WaitMsBeforeAsync":500,"toolAction":"Check submitProcess in index.html","toolSummary":"Check submitProcess"}}]}
